      "category": "cooling",
      "title": "2.2L Ecotec Coolant Leak and Thermostat Housing Crack",
      "description": "The 2.2L Ecotec engine develops coolant leaks from the plastic thermostat housing, water outlet, and coolant elbows. These plastic components crack from heat cycling.",
      "solution": "Pressure-test the cooling system and inspect the 2.2L Ecotec thermostat housing/water outlet assembly, coolant elbows, and nearby hose connections for seepage or visible cracks, especially around the plastic housing seam and mounting flange. Replace any cracked plastic thermostat housing or outlet components with updated OE-quality or aluminum aftermarket parts, install a new thermostat and seals/O-rings, then refill with the correct Dex-Cool coolant mixture and bleed air from the system. If overheating occurred, verify radiator fan operation and check for head gasket damage before returning the vehicle to service. Typical repair cost is about $150-$350 for housing/elbow replacement, or $300-$600 if multiple components and coolant service are needed.",
      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "symptoms": [
        "Coolant leak",
        "Low coolant warning",
        "Overheating",
        "Sweet smell from engine bay"
      ],
